### Fixed

- Avoid flagging component amount helpers as uncapped when a downstream derived output applies the same source limitation through that helper.
- Allow source-limitation validation for aggregate outputs that sum locally limited amount helpers.
- Recognize statutory `in excess of` progressive-tax brackets, collapse equal
  parenthetical currency restatements into one threshold, and bind established
  boundary helper names to their source-named tax base without accepting a
  different income or credit subject.
- Classify Alabama DHR POE SNAP manual outputs under a PolicyEngine oracle coverage prefix so bulk manual encodings do not fail repository validation as unmapped.
- Allow proof validation to recover flat alphabetic, numeric, and Roman subsection ownership without accepting sibling evidence.
- Keep attached amendment documents out of RuleSpec import guidance, identify
  them as proof-citation evidence for effective-dated rules in the target module,
  and steer retries when a corpus amendment path is emitted as an import.
- Tell the encoder to preserve amount-level treated-as-attributable rules as numeric outputs instead of boolean predicates.
- Repaired generated formula references like `input.foo` during apply validation.
- Preserve exact-oracle replacement surface visibility and typed inputs during
  apply-overlay validation, and reject new helper names that repeat a target
  path's year and legal-source identity.
- Repaired generated source-table interval bound parameters during apply validation.
- Prune generated unused imports during apply-overlay validation before revalidating generated RuleSpec artifacts.
- The waiver audit re-executes any expectation-violating module in isolation before reporting: concurrent fan-out occasionally perturbs an engine subprocess's outcome under load (observed ~1 per 3,099 modules per run), and a transient flake must not become a waiver accusation. The module's standalone value is the partition-invariant truth; real drift and stale waivers survive isolation, load flakes do not. Rechecked rows carry `isolated_recheck: true` in the report.
- Accept provenance-authenticated same-act deferrals that name a concrete unavailable dependency, including metadata-derived year-act references, while rejecting unrelated inputs and contradictory availability claims.
- Repair mismatched expectations in deterministic `auto_output_*` companion tests during `encode --apply`.
- Auto-repair preserves the consumer anchor when rewriting blocked synonyms on `#input.X` references in test YAML. Previously the repair unconditionally swapped the anchor to the canonical producer's location, corrupting input slot declarations by pointing them at the wrong file. Output (non-input) refs still get the anchor redirected to the canonical producer as before.
- Auto-repair blocked synonyms and bad anchors in generated `*.test.yaml` files before the apply gate fires, so a clean producer encode is not blocked by drift that only shows up in invented test cases. Producer YAML still fails loudly.
- Do not treat nested `_axiom` dependency workspaces inside country RuleSpec monorepos as canonical RuleSpec checkouts during upstream-placement validation.
- Classified Arizona CCAP as pending source ingestion in the PolicyEngine program surface report.
- Classify Arizona SNAP child support and medical deduction outputs in the PolicyEngine coverage registry.
- Batch fail-fast generated companion coverage repairs before engine validation and bound repair rounds so large source modules cannot spend hours revalidating one new case at a time.
- - Benchmark suite `allow_context` entries now point at the country-monorepo layout (`rulespec-us/us/statutes/...`, `rulespec-us/us/policies/...`) instead of the legacy pre-consolidation federal paths, so corpus-backed SNAP suites can resolve their repo-augmented context again.
- Repair apply-time handling for generated broad federal regulation range `implements` relations without concrete delegation bases.
- Classify California SSP's encoded chart amount as adjacent to PolicyEngine's final CA state supplement surface.
- Cache RuleSpec reference summaries and sibling rule-name inventories during validation so large changed-file batches do not repeatedly reparse the same target modules.
- Cache repeated source arithmetic topology parsing during complete-source validation and stream protected encoder diagnostics without buffering.
- Use absolute canonical-concept imports, include companion tests, and prefer imported child scalars when composing generated RuleSpec artifacts.
- Allow program-scope-sync to update canonical jurisdiction-local ProgramSpecs while retaining legacy top-level layout compatibility.
- Allow one signed targeted workflow run to freshly re-encode a bounded set of independent canonical RuleSpec modules, while preserving full-checkout validation and exact per-lane provenance and publication inventory checks.
- Keep the targeted signed re-encode workflow within GitHub's 25-input dispatch limit by using one bounded, mutually exclusive atomic-source input for source composition and canonical refresh transactions, while preserving legacy and new repair-artifact compatibility.
- Scope authenticated canonical replacement validation to the active jurisdiction and its country ancestors, so unrelated pre-hard-cut state paths cannot block a protected repair while fresh encodes continue to validate the complete checkout.
- Canonicalized shared statutory applicable-percentage names that use section-prefixed local names, preserving helper suffixes such as `_by_ratio_band`.
- Guide the encoder to apply alternative cap amounts to an uncapped base instead of substituting one cap branch for the base computation.
- Repair generated parent helpers that re-encode child-fragment numeric outputs during signed apply.
- Use generated relative output paths when repairing child numeric reencoding aliases during apply.
- Preserve explicit source-stated unit scope when apply repairs generated person-level rules.
- Generate CHIP FCEP eligibility formulas only for source-backed FCEP states instead of consuming a same-module availability flag at execution time.
- Generate CHIP FCEP availability as a derived source-backed boolean so FCEP judgment formulas can execute with state-set FPL parameters.
- Generate factual negative CHIP FCEP companion coverage so FCEP eligibility rules are covered without stubbing state-set parameters.
- Generate CHIP FCEP companion tests that pass state-set FCEP parameters as inputs when formulas depend on them.
- Generate CHIP FCEP companion tests as source-backed parameter assertions instead of stubbing generated parameter outputs into eligibility tests.
