- Derive PolicyEngine oracle-coverage output IDs through the jurisdiction-aware repo-routing helpers so country-monorepo checkouts (`rulespec-us/us-al/...`) produce the same `us-al:policies/X#name` IDs as legacy standalone checkouts instead of jurisdiction-doubled `us:us-al/...` IDs, unblocking the country-monorepo consolidation runs.
- Create missing country-monorepo jurisdiction directories before source encodes so first-time state encodings validate and apply under the correct jurisdiction root.
- Tell the encoder not to flatten thresholded or base-limited cited rates into flat current-source percentages.
- Scoped partial child-rewiring prompt guidance to the requested legal fragment and clarified that cross-reference exceptions should not cause whole-formula deferral when the target source states an executable formula.
- Include ancestor RuleSpec files when an explicit cross-section citation points to a deeper provision whose exact file does not exist.
- Route Danish corpus citations through a strict da-DK numeric grounding profile with decimal-comma rates, dot-grouped amounts, Danish percentage and currency markers, and legal-structure typing. The profile now uses an equal-length structural mask with identity provenance, snaps mask edges to numeric envelopes, and stops marker and unary-sign scans at mask boundaries. Standalone markers use a closed neighbor allowlist whose wrappers are transparent only when their full outward delimiter run is detached. Numeric continuation consumes only zero-width joiner, zero-width non-joiner, word joiner, soft hyphen, and byte-order mark inside one raw-exact numeral; other format characters act as token boundaries, and continuation shares the envelope grammar for decimal, grouping, and exponent forms, including failed exponent transitions and atomic malformed separator runs. Danish negative signs are joined only across those five format characters, so whitespace-prefixed prose negatives retain their sign while spaced range operators do not. Danish Markdown table-header context was removed: constructed pipe tables without an adjacent currency marker now fail closed, accepting the prior table-starvation case as intended fail-closed behavior. The 1,922-row live corpus contains no pipe characters, so the removal has zero live-corpus impact; the pre-existing 533/533 dot-group magnitude gate remains passing.
- Require generated bare local formula facts to be declared in the RuleSpec module's top-level input contract, and include that requirement in source-completeness retry feedback.
- Defer generated outputs that depend on unrelated same-section term imports during signed apply repair.
- Strengthen encoder prompts for deferred child branches and per-unit caps.
- Repair generated deferred output targets that place subsection labels between two hash separators.
- Teach encoder prompts that deferred outputs for omitted subsections must use child RuleSpec paths, and reject local numeric placeholders for rates or percentages set by upstream cross-references.
- Defer generated generic outputs during apply when validation finds they overlap deferred purpose-specific limitations.
- Reject dict-shaped deferred `source_values` entries so apply-time repair removes malformed generated metadata.
- Repair generated deferred outputs with prose `source_values` before signed apply validation.
- Repair generated SNAP delegated policy-setting source relations before signed apply.
- Accept digit-plus-scale monetary source phrases such as "20 million Euros" when grounding expanded numeric RuleSpec literals.
