- Ignore explicit bodyless repealed leaf tombstones when composing current-law parent corpus text.
- Fail CI when encoder-affecting changes are not behind an axiom-encode version bump.
- Rerun generated invalid companion-test input cleanup after test-input assignment repairs so newly exposed stale imported inputs do not block signed apply.
- Rerun generated invalid companion-test input repair after canonical test-reference repair.
- Interleave bounded validator findings from recent failed encode attempts so one diagnostic flood cannot evict all earlier rejected patterns.
- Keep bounded encoder repairs running when a generated retry cannot be overlaid onto its retained candidate, so duplicate names or malformed YAML become validator feedback instead of aborting the remaining attempts.
- Advance the artifact-only protected re-encode bridge to the exact reviewed RuleSpec US head pinned to the corrected Louisiana corpus release.
- Permit artifact-only targeted signed re-encodes from the exact independently reviewed RuleSpec US migration head while continuing to require main ancestry for PR-publishing runs.
- Rewrite `<producer>#input.X` to `<producer>#X` when a generated test case uses the input-slot shape to override an imported producer's output. The producer file does not declare X as an input slot (X is its output), so the runtime rejects the prefixed form. Runs before the existing remove-invalid-import-output-refs repair so the test keeps its override instead of losing the value entirely.
- Repair generated one-row entity tests that assert row-ordered outputs without creating the corresponding table row.
- Prefer configured RuleSpec roots over incidental sibling checkouts during compile validation.
- Tolerate tiny decimal residue when comparing RuleSpec numeric test outputs.
- Fix upstream placement validation for country-monorepo target aliases.
- Cache canonical RuleSpec checkout admission, symlink audits, Git identity probes, and target resolution for each bounded validation command so full-repository validation and waiver audits complete without repeating repository-wide work for every reference.
- Prefer explicit `AXIOM_RULESPEC_REPO_ROOTS` when resolving cross-repo RuleSpec targets, avoiding stale sibling checkouts shadowing configured roots during apply repairs.
- Fixed `axiom-encode test` for temporary RuleSpec checkouts whose directory name differs from the canonical repository name, and classified 26 USC 3211(b) RRTA tier 2 employee-representative tax as not comparable to PolicyEngine.
- Tolerate tiny decimal residue in the `axiom-encode test` companion-test runner.
- Copied precise nested same-section RuleSpec context for references such as `subsection (a)(7)(B)` before falling back to broader subsection context, and only require same-section imports when the cited RuleSpec source exists locally.
- Copy same-section subsection context for references such as "under subsection (y)", not only "subsection (y) of this section".
- Repair apply-time generated companion tests that assert scalar parameters or outputs before the RuleSpec output has a live version, and classify Colorado pension-subtraction outputs for PolicyEngine oracle coverage.
- Repair generated scalar relation rows when validation reports the resulting missing child input assignment.
- Scope source-subparagraph coverage to the actual requested workspace: pick the manifest matching the rules file (not first alphabetical) and accept human USC citations like `7 USC 2014(c)` in `requested_source`. Without this, validating sibling subsection encodes under a shared /tmp eval root silently loads the wrong workspace's metadata and rejects out-of-scope subparagraphs.
- Reject generated scoped exception amounts that are not gated by a source-stated category predicate.
- Strengthen encoder guidance for scoped exception predicates and source-gate companion test coverage.
- Ignore section-symbol legal citations such as `§ 435.121` when checking source numeric occurrence coverage.
- Allow multiline source-table selector result keys when they are backed by indexed parameter table keys.
- Defer generated sibling-name collisions during apply and remove stale local test outputs that no longer resolve after deferral.
- Skip the per-attempt generalist reviewer in `encode` once compile or CI validation has already rejected the candidate; the retry loop only feeds deterministic findings back, so the reviewer call was pure latency on every repair round.
- Allow a pristine paused SNAP queue to move to a newer signed corpus release, reviewed RuleSpec tip, and rules engine only when CI regenerates the complete queue from exact authenticated inputs.
- Tightened derived-relation prompt guidance so filtered entities such as `SnapUnit` are only used when the source defines membership and the file declares or imports the derived relation.
- Accept bare and finite Louisiana session-law repeal tombstones plus exact Louisiana delegated-rate dependencies in complete-source-unit validation.
- Reject synthetic `source_authorized` local inputs that make source-stated prohibitions or non-entitlements pass positive Judgment companion tests.
- Allow source-backed ASCII fraction parameter formulas and extracted source-backed parameter equality checks through the embedded scalar literal guard.
- Accept concrete source-bound missing-input and runtime-capability deferrals when they cite the exact current USC branch, while rejecting vague, wrong-branch, wrong-section, and source-unrelated claims.
- Validate and checkpoint signed canonical replacement targets before applying source bundles, while requiring legacy path migrations to complete in a separate signed transaction.
- Repair source-subparagraph coverage gaps by adding canonical child corpus citations to matching generated rule sources.
- Classify complete-source exception evidence by executable obligation type,
  including multiline selectors, enabling eligibility conditions, asserted
  unconditional non-applicability, formal cross-references, and arithmetic
  formula clauses. Diagnostics now identify each missing isolated case pair.
- Require proof-bound, version-aligned execution evidence for same-source condition
  gates and lower-bound clamps, rejecting opaque aggregate statuses, borrowed or
  shadow clamp witnesses, and unbounded dependency expansion.
- Repair missing source proof atoms in RuleSpec files whose rules sequence was normalized without item indentation.
- Repair generated implementation source relations that omit required delegation basis metadata during signed apply.
- Repair apply overlays that reduce duplicate-only generated modules to source_relation restatements instead of invalid empty modules.
- Strengthened source-scope validation to use rule-local proof excerpts before module summaries, catch definite person/member subjects encoded at unit scope, flag clear unrelated unit-to-unit mismatches, and recognize additional state-manual source wording.
- Guide encodings to keep source-stated cap and base formulas executable with legal boundary inputs when external bases or branch facts are unavailable.
- Repair generated source-table interval bounds named with adjacent band min/max suffixes.
- Reject source table encodings that expose structural band bounds as standalone scalar parameters.
- Repair generated source-table band threshold scalars before RuleSpec apply validation.
- Reject source table encodings that explode interval rows into one scalar parameter per row or cell instead of indexed parameter tables.
- Classify federal SSI income-exclusion RuleSpec outputs against PolicyEngine oracle coverage, including exact mappings for the general and earned-income exclusion parameters, and repair oracle parameter tests for simple source-backed fraction formulas.
- Treat compact US state-code citations as structural numeric evidence so complete-source validation does not require fake scalar rules for citation components.
- Matched eval source metadata by corpus paths so state encodes do not validate against unrelated fallback manifests.
- Preserve mapped oracle interfaces, temporal and clamp evidence, flattened statutory structure, and complete retry diagnostics when encoding state income tax rules.
- Prevent legal citations from becoming false source branches, recognize progressive
  tax clamps as boundary witnesses, and preserve pre-deferral tax-band rules during
