- Require complete-source-unit validation for every protected targeted signed re-encode so partial source coverage cannot be signed and proposed for merge.
- Remove the duplicate checkout identity from targeted signed re-encodes now that the protected runtime supplies a byte-bound encoder attestation.
- Defer generated outputs that treat tax-status or marital-status legal classifications as local factual inputs during signed apply.
- Recognize mixed-fraction percentage language without treating its fractional
  word as a separate arithmetic obligation, and resolve bounded, input-free,
  period-aware parameter aliases when validating formula evidence. Propagate
  authoritative source proof through reached temporal aliases, fail closed on
