  verify a legacy RuleSpec path replacement.
- Classify UK Universal Credit housing schedule helper outputs for PolicyEngine oracle coverage.
- Reject generated outputs that expose a local "shall not apply" exception without negating it in the matching `*_applies` rule.
- Defer generated outputs that depend on same-repo import fragments absent from the referenced RuleSpec file instead of treating the fragment as a local factual input during apply.
- Normalize legal citation dash variants when matching complete-source deferrals to RuleSpec target paths.
- Normalize Unicode dash punctuation to ASCII hyphens across canonical, alias, and structured RuleSpec output paths while preserving authoritative corpus citation identifiers.
- Reject generated imports that borrow another section's same-named term when the current section already defines or defers that term.
- Keep explicit currency thresholds from being reinterpreted as rates merely
